    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0526" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A4B/618</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the French Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Laboulaye</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-12">January 12,
                        1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of Your Excellency’s note of January 2, 1935, in which you quote a
                    communication received from your Government with respect to the notification by
                    Japan of intention to terminate the Washington Naval Treaty. The statement that
                    the French Government would not have been able in any case to agree to a
                    continuance (<hi rendition="#italic">réconduction</hi>) of the present Treaty is
                    a source of surprise and disappointment. For its part, this Government has
                    indicated regret at the prospective termination of the Treaty, and has fully set
                    forth its views in the statement which I made on the occasion of Japanese
                    notification on December 29, last, as well as in Mr. Davis’ speech in London on
                    December 6, copies of which I take pleasure in attaching.</p>
                <p>I should be glad, however, to have you thank the Minister of Foreign Affairs for
                    his courtesy in frankly informing me of the French Government’s views, of which
                    I have taken careful note.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
